course: dictionary
lesson: 9207
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word soldier can mean different things, so check the context before you decide. A soldier is a member of an army, trained to fight for their country. In «Napoleon's soldiers came» to the Sphinx, the clue is the army, so the word means people who fight.
explain: Soldier can also be a verb. To soldier on means to keep going when things are hard or you feel ill. If someone has a sore throat and still finishes the race, you could say they soldiered on. Ask yourself: is this word a person, or an action?
explain: In the UK, «soldiers» can also mean thin strips of toast for dipping into a boiled egg. The clue here is the egg, so the meaning is food. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: A soldier is a member of an army who is trained to fight for their country.
fact: To soldier on means to keep going even when things are hard or you feel ill.
fact: «Egg and soldiers» is a snack of a boiled egg with thin strips of toast to dip in.
fact: In «toy soldiers», the word means small models of soldiers, not real people.
fact: On Remembrance Day, people remember soldiers who died in wars.
exercise: «The procession had ten soldiers carrying clubs.» What is a soldier in this sentence? | A thin strip of toast | *A person in an army, trained to fight | A kind of boiled egg
exercise: Ben is ill, but he keeps going. His mum says, «You're soldiering on, love.» What does soldiering on mean? | Stopping to rest for a whole day | *Keeping going even when things are hard | Singing loudly with the band
exercise: Ella says, «I want soldiers with my egg, please.» What does soldiers mean here? | *Thin strips of toast to dip in the egg | Toy soldiers in a box | People who fight in wars | Clay statues of a king's army
test: Toad is taken past «soldiers and guard-dogs» into a grim old castle. What are the soldiers doing there? | Playing cards in the hall | *Guarding the castle | Growing vegetables in the garden | Selling carrots in the market
test: The Terracotta Army has thousands of life-size clay «soldiers» with different faces. What are these soldiers? | Real people from a farm | Strips of toast | Toy cars in a box | *Statues of soldiers, made from clay
exam: Many countries sent weapons, training and money to Ukraine's army but did not send their own «soldiers» to fight. What does soldiers mean here? | *People who are members of an army | Thin strips of toast | Shiny statues made of clay | Players in a card game
